# Source of truth

| Information | Canonical owner |
| --- | --- |
| Shared agent behavior | [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md) |
| Current focus and next work | [PROJECT_STATE.md](../PROJECT_STATE.md) |
| Identity and accepted project scope | [Project Brief](../Project%20Brief.md) |
| Domain-specific intent and rules | Owner selected in [Domain Index](Domain%20Index.md) |
| Accepted durable decisions | Records linked from [Decisions](Decisions/Index.md) |
| Execution progress and handoff | [Work](Work/Index.md) |
| Structured configuration/numeric data | Not designated; resolve when needed |
| Code and runtime evidence | Not designated; resolve when needed |
| Visual/design assets | Not designated; resolve when needed |
| Playtest/analytics evidence | Not designated; resolve when needed |

Design describes intended behavior; code/config and observations describe their
respective implemented or measured state. A mismatch is a finding to resolve,
not permission to silently rewrite one to match the other. Keep volatile tables
in the designated structured source and link their meaning here.

The installed plugin owns reusable workflow guidance; this KB owns project facts
and accepted local rules. No external tool, storage provider or source location
is selected merely because a template mentions that category.
